        "code": {
          "text": "Globus pharyngeus / non-specific throat sensation, likely functional related to stress and voice strain; possible reflux component"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Condition/condition-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Condition",
        "id": "condition-2",
        "clinicalStatus": {
          "coding": [
            {
              "system": "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/condition-clinical",
              "code": "active"
            }
          ]
        },
        "code": {
          "text": "Moderate premenstrual syndrome, predominantly mood symptoms and irritability"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-1",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Throat sensation and associated symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intermittent tight sensation in the throat, especially in the evenings when lying down, occurring 4–5 days per week; feels like something is stuck. No true pain, dysphagia to solids or fluids, odynophagia, choking, or regurgitation. Similar globus episodes during stress in the past."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-2",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Hoarseness"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild intermittent hoarseness, especially after a full day teaching or yelling."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated throat and constitutional symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No coryzal symptoms, cough, fevers, weight loss, or night sweats."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-4",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-4",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Premenstrual symptoms and timing"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Longstanding irritability, marked mood swings, bloating, breast tenderness, and headaches during the week before menses; symptoms settle 1–2 days after bleeding starts, with the patient essentially well mid-cycle. Cycles regular at 28–30 days, bleeding 5–6 days. A symptom diary is only partly completed for one cycle; the recorded pattern is luteal-phase symptoms resolving after menses."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-5",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mood symptoms and safety"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports feeling like she will snap at everyone in the week before her period, with increased conflict at work and with her partner. PMS physical symptoms are milder than mood symptoms and irritability. No persistent low mood or anhedonia outside the premenstrual week; no suicidal ideation, self-harm, or psychosis."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Other reported mood and stress symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports being somewhat more short-fused through the month since starting a new class; this was not explored further. Reports increased stress this term and anxiety about possible thyroid disease or cancer after searching online."
      }
    },
